Title: Gaze close refuses review trees holding its own setup copies (.env, .dvc/config.local)
Created: 2026-10-31
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-10-31T21:00Z claude created

--- body ---
## Context

Observed 2026-10-31 in climate-finance-het, PR #2003 (ticket 2723), two gaze runs in a row:
`gaze_close.py` refused to remove `.claude/worktrees/review-2003` because `worktree_residue`
(scripts/worktree-clean-lib.sh) flags ignored entries that gaze setup itself placed there from
the project's `.worktreeinclude`, plus files the test seats wrote:
`.env` and `.dvc/config.local` (byte-identical to the primary checkout's), `.venv` and
`.dvc/cache` (symlinks to the primary), `.pytest_cache/`, `__pycache__/`, empty `data/pool/istex/`,
and two regenerated `deliverables/_shared/figures/fig_lexical_tfidf_*.png`.
The review content was PASS (panel, no blocking finding), but the answer is recorded ESCALATE,
so verify-gate refuses (`review_notes.py gate`: "latest gaze answer is ESCALATE") and the PR
cannot merge without the author. The leftover tree also blocks the next gaze's setup (exit 1).
Commit 3948d6cb (ticket 1357) tolerated setuptools build output and an untracked .venv only.

Impact: in any project with a `.worktreeinclude`, every gaze that runs tests ends ESCALATE;
merges stall on a cleanup artifact.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] A review tree holding only setup-made copies (byte-identical files or symlinks into the
      primary checkout, per `.worktreeinclude`) and tool caches is removed by gaze close without
      ESCALATE; a hand-made ignored file still stays residue
- [ ] Red test replays this case (copied .env + .dvc/config.local + symlinked .venv/.dvc/cache)
- [ ] Decide how test-written ignored outputs (regenerated figures, empty data dirs) are treated;
      do not silently delete anything not provably a copy or cache

## Same root cause in roar (added 2026-10-31)

`skills/roar/close-and-clean.sh --phase exit-check` reports `PREFLIGHT: DIRTY` / `EXIT: KEEP-PENDING`
on a fresh roar bundle tree whose only ignored entries are `.env`, `.dvc/config.local`
(byte-identical to the primary, listed in `.worktreeinclude`) and the `.venv` / `.dvc/cache`
symlinks into the primary. So roar can remove no worktree in a project with `.worktreeinclude`.
Exit criterion 1 covers roar's preflight as well as gaze close.
